<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for Umber.

  A terminal app inherits every capability request from whatever the user runs inside
  it, so the entitlements here are the ones the SHELL process needs, not the ones a
  typical GUI app would request.

  com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit
    JIT compilation. Required by some programs the user may run (node, bun, etc.) and
    harmless when unused.

  com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
    mmap(PROT_WRITE|PROT_EXEC) without code-signing the page first. Some interpreters
    and JIT engines (Python, Ruby, Lua) allocate executable memory this way. Without
    this, those programs segfault inside Umber but work fine in Terminal.app.

  com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
    Load dylibs/bundles not signed by the same team. Required because:
    1. GhosttyKit.xcframework is a prebuilt upstream binary signed by Ghostty's team.
    2. Users may run programs that dlopen third-party libraries.
    Without this, the hardened runtime refuses to load GhosttyKit at all.

  The TCC keys (microphone, desktop, etc.) are in Info.plist, not here — those are
  usage-description strings, not entitlements.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
